<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Syrian Federation</h1><p class="st-meta">1922 CE – 1924 CE · capital Aleppo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived federation of the French-created Syrian states, a step towards reuniting Syria under the mandate.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In June 1922 the French high commissioner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henri-gouraud">Henri Gouraud</a> united the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-damascus">State of Damascus</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-aleppo">State of Aleppo</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alawite-state">Alawite State</a> in a federation, a partial response to nationalist demands for unity.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A federal council of delegates from the three states, under the presidency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subhi-barakat">Subhi Barakat</a>, handled common affairs, while each state kept its own government and French officials held real power. The capital alternated between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>. The federation had a single budget, customs and currency, but nationalists criticised it as a French device that kept <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lebanese-republic">Lebanon</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabal-al-druze">Jabal Druze</a> and Alexandretta apart from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alawite-state">Alawite State</a> withdrew at the start of 1925.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>At the end of 1924 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> dissolved the federation, merging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-syria">State of Syria</a> from January 1925.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/syrian-federation.jpg" alt="Syrian Federation" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: F l a n k e r · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Syria_French_mandate.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1922 CE – 1924 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Aleppo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Subhi Barakat</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Federation of Syrian States</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1923&amp;focus=syrian-federation" aria-label="Syrian Federation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5616 871 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Syrian Federation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5936 1127L5905 1205M5936 1127L5927 1218"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5905 1205h0M5927 1218h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5936 1127h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5936 1127h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Aleppo. <a href="/atlas?year=1923&amp;focus=syrian-federation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
